before:
```typescript
type PersonName = { name: string };
function nameText(person: PersonName): string {
  return person.name;
}
const visitor = { name: "Asha", visits: 3 };
console.log(nameText(visitor));
console.log(visitor.visits);
```
This prints Asha, then 3. nameText receives an object with a text name and returns that field. visitor also has visits; passing it does not remove visits. console.log displays each supplied value on its own line.

